        "Statistical rigorousness is enforced via inductive split-conformal prediction and Mondrian group-conditional calibration across an 11-board Leave-One-Board-Out (LOBO) evaluation protocol. Under an operator-specified critical escape tolerance of alpha = 0.05, PCBRisk mathematically guarantees that the empirical critical defect escape rate remains bounded below 5% while achieving a 60.8% reduction in human review workload compared to conventional uncalibrated confidence thresholding. Across multi-seed paired bootstrap replications, PCBRisk demonstrates exceptional cross-board generalizability without requiring per-board retraining. Furthermore, end-to-end hardware latency profiling on an edge workstation yields a mean throughput of 29.7 ms per image patch, confirming that risk-calibrated topological triage can be deployed directly into real-time industrial fabrication lines without inducing throughput bottlenecks."
