        "When operator fatigue sets in, the probability of human verification error escalates dramatically. Studies in industrial ergonomics indicate that human defect miss rates increase by upwards of 30% over the course of an 8-hour shift. To mitigate false alarm floods, manufacturing engineers frequently adjust global confidence thresholds upward; however, this ad-hoc practice creates the catastrophic risk of defect escapes—allowing severe open circuits or conductive bridges to slip into finished goods. PCBRisk fundamentally re-engineers this paradigm by combining high-speed neural defect localization with local circuit graph topology and rigorous split-conformal risk bounds, transforming optical inspection from a heuristic classification task into a mathematically guaranteed decision-theoretic triage framework."
