        "Furthermore, contemporary electronics contract manufacturers operate under wafer-thin profit margins (typically 2% to 6%), where inspection labor and false-alarm scrap represent major cost centers. In high-volume consumer electronics lines producing 50,000 boards per day, an AOI false reject rate of merely 3% generates 1,500 false scrap events or requires continuous round-the-clock manual operator re-screening. Standard computer vision models lack the context to distinguish between an alarming-looking surface discoloration on an isolated ground flood plane (which carries zero electrical consequence) and a sub-pixel trace narrowing in a high-speed differential clock line (which creates high-frequency signal attenuation or an open circuit). By bridging visual object detection with circuit topology and conformal risk control, PCBRisk provides the exact mathematical and operational framework required to slash human review overhead while eliminating defect escapes."
